<title>USA: PSE&amp;G to shut 1,031 MW N.J. nuke unit Sat.</title>
<headline>PSE&amp;G to shut 1,031 MW N.J. nuke unit Sat.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Enterprise Group Inc said Thursday it will shut for one week beginning Saturday its 1,031 megawatt (MW) Hope Creek nuclear unit in Salem, New Jersey, for valve repairs.  </p>
<p>&quot;It should be reducing power Friday. It should come off line Saturday,&quot; a company spokeswoman said, adding Public Service planned to perform repair on valves in the reactor's recirculating system.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a brief outage...It's going to last seven days,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Public Service Enterprise is the operator and majority owner of the Hope Creek.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
